iterations.notes:
My diagnosis is that the mustard bottle slips by twisting, not by sliding straight down. Linear friction, about 21.6 N, is roughly three times the load, but the 191 mm bottle can pivot about the squeeze axis if it is gripped off its centre of mass. The only pads change the record has rewarded is more width, while moves on reach and tilt kept losing the dice or potted meat. So all three proposals keep the pad tilt (8.8°), reach (3 mm) and groove (3.34 mm) that hold the dice, and make the contact patch bigger:
- the widest pad (24 mm);
- the widest pad plus a slightly thicker TPU skin (1.31 → 2.0 mm), which is a bit riskier for the dice;
- a middle width (20 mm) as a fallback.

All three cost $0 and only need a reprint of a few grams. I'm not proposing a swap or a new part, because the prismatic jaw already holds its fingertips level and its face angle the same at every opening.
